  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want a burst of session changes to cost one reload, so that whatever fires `currentSessionChanges` again (the #1276 loop was one such source) can never multiply requests. Audit #1388, finding A2: the amplifier of the #1276 loop is still there after #1385.\n\n### What happens (read at `dev-swift` `1685bcc`)\n- `RootNavigationView.swift:44-47`: `.onChange(of: accounts?.currentSessionChanges) { Task { await model.currentSessionChanged(expired:) } }`: one unstructured task per bump, per window.\n- `RootModel.currentSessionChanged` (`RootModel.swift:311-315`) reloads the home page, then every shown list of Catégories and Favoris (`NavigationModel.sessionDidChange`, `NavigationModel.swift:92-98`: the selection and a pushed category, each).\n- Nothing limits it: N bumps = N home GETs + N × (1 to 4) list GETs, each superseding the one before (`ContentLoader.load` cancels the task in flight, so the earlier requests leave and are cancelled).\n\n### Failing scenario and count\nDevice trace of #1276 (issuecomment-7218471693): 11 bumps in 2.4 s → 12 `/` + 12 `/forum1f.php`, 6 cancelled in flight. Per bump the budget is 2 requests on an iPhone showing Favoris, up to 5 with a list open in both tabs, times the number of windows on an iPad (each window has its own `RootModel`).\n\nThe bump sources today: `checkSessions` `.expired` (`AccountsModel.swift:223`), a re-login in place (`:270`), the sync take-over (`:431`).\n\n### Proposed fix\n- One reload at a time per root: a bump while a reload runs marks it dirty, and one more reload runs at the end (never one per bump).\n- A floor between two session-change reloads (e.g. 2 s) as a fuse, with the last bump always honoured.\n- Test (app, counting `ForumDataSource`): 10 bumps in one main-actor turn → at most 2 home loads and 2 loads per shown list.\n\nRefs #1388, #1276, #1385.",
